  "scientificScope": [
    "Two exposed operations: BAM-reference coverage and nonoverlapping target BED depth/breadth. Accurate upstream CIGAR processing and proper-pair overlap correction, with explicit MAPQ/flag masks and no base-quality filter.",
    "Independent synthetic truth covers deletions, splice gaps, pair overlap, low MAPQ, Q0 bases, secondary/duplicate/QC-failed/supplementary flags, empty regions/contigs/BAM, full denominators, and threads 1/2/4.",
    "The primary summary is a separately identified streaming length-weighted aggregation of upstream per-base intervals over every BAM dictionary/target base. Raw upstream observed-contig summary/distributions remain unchanged; their denominators can differ.",
    "The Linux suite also compares raw scientific output with the hash-pinned official unmodified mosdepth 0.3.14 binary under four configurations."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Native installation checks use the actual released Workbench bridge/importer/scientific runner; graph/archive tests use a copy-based publication callback and do not themselves execute the native importer or scientific programs. Direct installed-PE regression execution is recorded separately.",
    "Research/teaching synthetic validation; no clinical, diagnostic, regulatory or institutional approval claim. No whole-human-genome/resource-performance benchmark.",
    "No interactive desktop GUI, cancellation, Unicode/long-path or Windows network-firewall test. Ordinary and space-containing ASCII Windows paths were exercised. Analysis exposes only explicit local BAM/BED files; CRAM, SAM and remote analyses are not exposed.",
    "The BAM reference dictionary defines denominators; assembly identity is not verified against FASTA. All BAM samples/read groups are aggregated. RNA BAM coverage is genomic coverage, not differential expression.",
    "Mosdepth requires roughly four bytes times the longest contig length, plus overhead. Workbench stages a full BAM copy, creates CSI and retains potentially large per-base BGZF output.",
    "Three-line boundary patch fixes report precision, ignores implicit REF_PATH for BAM-only use and labels the runtime; coverage algorithms are unchanged.",
    "Publisher identity is not authenticated by offline SHA/inventory verification. The signed catalogue/trust deployment is a separate unfinished project task."
  ]
}
